<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices firmed on good demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices firmed on good demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices firmed on Tuesday on better demand, rising by 100 to 150 rupees per tonne, dealers said.</p>
<p>Plant delvery prices were steady and arrivals were around 20,000 tonnes in central Indian markets.</p>
<p>Soybean yellow was traded in the 10,000-10,400 rupees per tonne range in the markets while it was at 10,250-10,600 per tonne in plant delivered condition.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady in a very limited trade. The undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on good exports demand against limited selling from Indian exporters.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $278 to $279 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Shift) on Tuesday against $214 to $215 in the same period last year. Rapeseed extraction was $130 per tonne in export, while rapeseed extraction was 4,500 rupees for Bedibunder and was 4,450 rupees to 4,475 rupees for Bhavnager.</p>
